model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.accountPresentation {
    metadata {
      constraint "A generated or blank account label never titles a row. After a verified identity, an authored name and a check-reported email, display name or username, an account saved without a name is titled by its provider and the first part of its declared kind, such as \"Example API key\", keeping the generated number so \"Default 2\" stays distinct as \"Example API key 2\"; an unknown kind reads \"account\", and without a provider name the caller's fallback keeps the number. Lists that know only an app's requirements take the kind from the requirement for the account's provider, so the Accounts list, app Accounts tabs, pickers, the tool runner and account dialogs name an account the same way. No fragment of a credential is shown or stored for this. While a dialog waits for its account read it names the exact binding the person picked, by its saved name or else its own row title without the group's verified identity. The stored label and its Manage control are unchanged."
    }
  }
}
